"""29 October 2026 : ZenRay Lines TUBE NET, the curve network of one tube of a mannequin (a finger, a limb) from its geometry alone.
EN: a tube is a branch of the merge tree of the geodesic distance (ZrlTubes.py). Its rings are contours of the distance (exact loops on the surface, perpendicular to the tube),
its seams are the lines of constant angle around the tube axis through those rings. Rings and seams cross at corner nodes ; the faces between two rings and two seams are four
sided patches with matching borders, so the network meshes into clean quads. The tip is closed by a ring of three sided patches around the tip point.
Nothing here is specific to a finger : a limb is the same call with another ring step.
    python -I ZrlTubeNet.py --obj model.obj --out doc.json [--fingers] [--ring-mm 12]
FR : les anneaux (contours de distance) et les coutures (lignes à angle constant) d'un tube, noeuds aux croisements, faces à quatre côtés.
"""
